{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1937 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "da63a2f827934f4ee49d3a55e26929e48ad890456a50da8d626d9343be68a8fe" :edb/db-before-t 1936 :edb/db-after-t 1937 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535249 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:25:27.298Z" 13194139535249 true] [17592186339818 1100 "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}\\,i-\\frac{2}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $9x^2+4y^2=36$, oriented counterclockwise. Interpret circulation here as the sum of the four convergent improper line integrals on the open quadrant arcs, taking the one-sided limits independently at each axis intersection. The field is undefined at $(\\pm2,0)$ and $(0,\\pm3)$; ordinary circulation on the entire closed ellipse is not defined as stated in the original source." 13194139535249 true] [17592186339818 1100 "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}\\,i-\\frac{2}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$ oriented counterclockwise." 13194139535249 false] [17592186339818 1145 "First, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $3,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{3}{y}\\,i-\\frac{2}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-2-3 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-5)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-5(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-10\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535249 false] [17592186339818 1145 "The field is undefined where $x=0$ or $y=0$, so the original prompt does not define an ordinary line integral over all of $C$. Under the explicit improper-integral interpretation, parameterize counterclockwise by\n\n$$r(t)=(2\\cos t,3\\sin t),\\qquad 0\\le t\\le2\\pi.$$\n\nFor $t$ strictly inside each of the four quadrant intervals, both coordinates are nonzero and\n\n$$\\frac{3}{y}\\,dx=\\frac{3}{3\\sin t}(-2\\sin t)\\,dt=-2\\,dt,\\qquad -\\frac{2}{x}\\,dy=-\\frac{2}{2\\cos t}(3\\cos t)\\,dt=-3\\,dt.$$\n\nThus the pulled-back integrand is exactly $-5$ on each open arc. At every excluded endpoint its one-sided limit is $-5$, so every individual improper integral converges; no cancellation between divergent integrals or principal-value convention is needed. With $a_k=k\\pi/2$,\n\n$$\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{imp}}=\\sum_{k=0}^{3}\\lim_{\\epsilon\\downarrow0,\\,\\delta\\downarrow0}\\int_{a_k+\\epsilon}^{a_{k+1}-\\delta}(-5)\\,dt=4\\left(-\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right)=-10\\pi.$$\n\nThe unchanged displayed option c is therefore correct for this explicit interpretation. This does not assign values to $F$ at the four axis intersections or establish ordinary circulation there." 13194139535249 true]] :edb/tempids {}}
